    "vernacular": "Post-war, rapidly grown Pacific capital on a narrow coastal strip: 1-3 storey cream or pastel-painted concrete-block buildings with deep verandas and corrugated-iron roofs (red, green, grey), timber and fibro houses on low stilts, Chinatown shophouses with high porches (partly rebuilt after 2006), and traditional leaf-roofed houses at the Cultural Centre. Hot, humid, dusty red-brown ground with coconut palms and tropical broadleaf trees against steep green ridges.",
